==Dutch==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|dum|nl}} {{term|nog|lang=dum}}, {{term|noch|lang=dum}}, from {{etyl|odt|nl}} {{term|nogh|lang=odt}}, {{term|noch||until now, still|lang=odt}}, from {{etyl|gem-pro|nl}} {{recons|nuh||still|lit=now too|lang=gem-pro}}, from {{etyl|ine-pro|nl}} {{recons|nu||now|lang=ine-pro}} + {{recons|-kʷe-||and, also|lang=ine-pro}}. Cognate with {{etyl|de|-}} {{term|noch||yet, still|lang=de}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|NL}} {{IPA|/nɔx/|/nɔχ/|lang=nl}}
*: {{audio|Nl-nog.ogg|audio}}
* {{a|BE}} {{IPA|/nɔç/|/nɔx/|lang=nl}}
* {{rhymes|ɔx|lang=nl}}

===Adverb===
{{nl-adv}}

# [[still]]
#: ''hij is nog nieuw'' &mdash; he's still a newbie
# with negation: [[yet]]
#: ''hij is nog niet gekomen'' &mdash; he has not come yet
# with [[een]]: [[another]]
#: ''daar is er nog een'' &mdash; there's another one

